      "x": 40,
      "y": 430,
      "width": 760,
      "height": 44,
      "strokeColor": "#495057",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "roundness": null,
      "text": "Miss cases (\u2192 output 0):  sky pixel (d > 0.9999) \u00b7 ray leaves screen \u00b7 past maxDist \u00b7 no depth intersection.\nOn a miss nothing is added, so the split-sum sky IBL already baked into the HDR is the graceful fallback.",
      "fontSize": 11,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top"
    }
